@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
title Behavior - Read bounded backlog and full priority count
actor "Authorized user" as actor
box "Frontend - Mission Control application" #E0F2FE
  participant "BacklogPage / BacklogView" as page
  participant "IWorkOrderService / WorkOrderService" as client
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Api" #D1FADF
  participant "CurrentAccountAuthorization" as access
  participant "WorkOrdersController" as ctrl
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "ValidationBehavior" as validation
  participant "ListBacklogQueryHandler" as handler
  participant "WorkOrder" as entity
end box
box "Backend - MissionControl.Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  database "Mission Control SQL" as db
end box
actor -> page : Open the Backlog tab, change page, or Reload backlog; a change of the view's refresh input rereads the same page
page -> page : BacklogView sets its query signal; resource status loading shows skeleton rows (loading state)
page -> client : BacklogView's backlogResource reads ListBacklogQuery (page, page size); a changed page aborts the superseded request
client -> access : GET /api/workspaces/{id}/backlog
access -> access : L2-002 validate signature, issuer, audience, subject, expiry
access -> db : Read current status, role and credential version
db --> access : Current account access
alt Missing, invalid or expired JWT; deactivated account
  access --> client : 401; audit denial without payloads
  client --> page : sessionInterceptor calls SessionService.end(Unauthorized) once for this generation; the read is cancelled; sign in returns to the backlog
else Authenticated (every role may read the backlog)
  access -> ctrl : Authorized request
  ctrl -> validation : Send ListBacklogQuery through MediatR 12.5.0
  validation -> validation : L2-045 page of 1 or more; page size 1-100, default 25
  alt Zero, negative, or over-100 page size
    validation --> ctrl : 400 page-size message; nothing read
    ctrl --> client : Validation ProblemDetails
    client --> page : Fall back to 25 per page and show the message
  else Valid request
    validation -> handler : Handle ListBacklogQuery
    handler -> db : L2-045 ListBacklogAsync: one page of BacklogItem rows without descriptions (epic and initiative titles, assignee name and active flag, estimate, open sprint and status, completedIn), ordered by priority then ID, with the full count, status totals, order version, sprintsPaused, and sprint targets (active sprint first, then up to 25 planned sprints) in one consistent read
    db --> handler : Bounded rows, full count, status totals, version
    alt Workspace not found (also when the project was deleted after the backlog opened)
      handler --> ctrl : 404
      ctrl --> client : ProblemDetails (not found)
      client --> page : BacklogView shows Project not found with Back to projects (no Try again or reference ID; focus its heading when the replaced rows held focus) and emits notFound; on the first one only BacklogPage calls the layout's refresh(), so the header rereads once and keeps only the breadcrumb
    else Rows read
      handler -> entity : Project ranks, open sprint and completedIn labels, and Add to sprint eligibility (NoSprints, SprintsPaused, NoOpenSprint, Done, InOpenSprint, or Eligible) for the delivery mode
      entity --> handler : Backlog page with absolute ranks
      handler --> ctrl : BacklogItemPage with items, total count, page, page size, status totals, sprint targets, sprintsPaused, and order version
      ctrl --> client : 200
      client --> page : Update signal state; zero stories shows the empty state, whose Add initiative emits addInitiativeRequested; on the first read, and whenever a read changes whether the total is zero, BacklogView emits emptyChange, and BacklogPage registers Add initiative as the header's tab action while it is true, Add story otherwise
      page --> actor : Present the page, totals for all stories, and the pager when there is more than one page; when sprintsPaused, the paused banner (Change delivery mode only with canChangeMode)
      opt Add to sprint from a row's menu
        actor -> page : Choose Sprint 8 (Active) or Sprint 9 (Planned) from sprintTargets
        page -> page : BacklogView emits addToSprintRequested (story ID, SprintTarget). Active: BacklogPage opens SprintScopeDialog in add mode (offerSprintsLink true), which preselects the story once its eligible read returns it; on SprintScopeOutcome Changed it rereads the backlog and shows the "Scope updated" toast with the outcome's summary, and on Outdated it rereads the backlog; while the dialog stays open its forbidden output (an unexpected 403) shows the "Your access changed" toast without Retry. Planned: BacklogPage navigates to /projects/:id/sprints/:sprintId/plan?add={storyId}, which marks the story To add; the backlog reads afresh on return
      end
    end
  end
end
opt Read fails unexpectedly (500 or 503 with correlation ID, or no response)
  client --> page : Error state with Try again and the reference ID only when the server answered; no stale rows shown as current; Try again emits retryRequested, so BacklogPage calls the layout's refresh() and a failed project header rereads with the tab
end
note over ctrl, db
Unexpected failures return generic 500 plus correlation ID (L2-043).
Totals come from persisted records, never from the loaded page.
Diagnostics exclude secrets and contact payloads.
end note
@enduml
